<section class="hero"><div class="container"><div class="hero-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">USC VITERBI · EE 641 · 2026 FALL</div><h1>Research,<br><span>with purpose.</span></h1><div class="hero-sub">从一个值得一起打磨的问题，到一套稳稳推进、可复现的深度学习实验。<span class="en">From a meaningful question to a thoughtful, reproducible deep learning project your team can grow together.</span></div><div class="hero-ctas"><a href="#compare" class="btn">一起看看五个选题 <span>↗</span></a><a href="#roadmap" class="btn ghost">浏览项目时间线 ↓</a></div></div><div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true"><div class="orbit"></div><div class="orbit two"></div><div class="orb"></div><div class="float-tag ft-a">01 &nbsp; Research hypothesis</div><div class="float-tag ft-b"><span class="bullet"></span> Reproducible results</div><div class="float-tag ft-c">05 &nbsp; Project directions</div></div></div><div class="hero-foot"><div><strong>05</strong>研究方向 / Research tracks</div><div><strong>02</strong>组员 / Teammates</div><div><strong>06</strong>核心要求 / Technical pillars</div><div><strong>06 <small style="font-size:11px">weeks</small></strong>示例计划 / Sample plan</div></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="overview"><div class="container"><div class="section-header"><div><div class="eyebrow">THE STRATEGY</div><h2>把问题想清楚，<br>模型自然会更从容。</h2></div><p>这门课更欣赏扎实、诚实、能解释清楚来龙去脉的项目。与其追求表面上“更大更强”，不如一起把问题、实验和结论慢慢打磨到清楚可信。<span class="en">The course values projects that are thoughtful, rigorous, and explainable. Rather than chasing the biggest model, aim for a study your team can understand deeply and present with confidence.</span></p></div><div class="summary-grid"><article class="surface feature-card"><span class="pill green">OUR LEADING PROPOSAL · 首推</span><h3>航拍场景中的<br>小目标检测</h3><span class="en" style="font-size:14px">Scale-aware feature fusion for aerial small-object detection</span><p>这是一个边界清楚、资料成熟、也很适合两人稳步推进的方向。它既有足够的技术深度，也方便把“效果”与“成本”之间的真实取舍讲清楚。<span class="en">This direction offers a clear scope, mature resources, and a healthy balance between technical depth and feasibility for a two-person team.</span></p><ul><li>Baseline：轻量级目标检测网络 / Lightweight detector</li><li>研究：特征融合与目标尺度 / Multi-scale feature design</li><li>指标：mAP、Recall、Latency、显存 / Memory</li></ul><button class="text-link" onclick="openTopic('aerial')">看看完整研究蓝图 / Open blueprint →</button></article><article class="surface minor-card"><div class="eyebrow">COURSE EXPECTATIONS</div><h3>课程真正鼓励什么？</h3><div class="rule"><b>技术深度</b><span>不是套用预训练模型 / Beyond a pretrained inference wrapper</span></div><div class="rule"><b>实验严谨</b><span>Baseline、控制变量、消融 / Baselines, controls, ablations</span></div><div class="rule"><b>关键洞察</b><span>成功、失败与泛化 / Success, failure, generalization</span></div><div class="rule"><b>完整执行</b><span>两人可实现并可复现 / Feasible and reproducible by two</span></div><div class="warning-strip">温柔提醒：官方指南里没有写明确切提交日期、Proposal 格式或评分百分比，这些信息还需要再去核对 <strong>Project Deliverables</strong>。<span class="en">A gentle note: the supplied PDF does not include exact deadlines, proposal format, or grading weights, so those details still need to be verified in Project Deliverables.</span></div></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="compare"><div class="container"><div class="section-header"><div><div class="eyebrow">DECISION MATRIX</div><h2>把五个方向放在一起，<br>慢慢看清。</h2></div><p>你们可以拖动权重，看看在不同偏好下，哪些方向更适合这学期的节奏。这里的分数只是帮助讨论的参考，不是教授的官方评分。<span class="en">Adjust the weights to see which ideas feel like the best fit for your team's goals. These scores are conversation aids, not official grades.</span></p></div><div class="ranking-layout"><aside class="surface settings-panel"><h3>看看你们更看重什么</h3><p class="helper">把关注点轻轻调一调，系统会自动归一化分数。<span class="en">Tune the priorities gently — weights are normalized automatically.</span></p><div class="weight-row"><div class="weight-top"><span>课程契合度 · Course fit</span><output id="w-course-out">35</output></div><input id="w-course" aria-label="课程契合度" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="35"></div><div class="weight-row"><div class="weight-top"><span>可完成性 · Feasibility</span><output id="w-feas-out">30</output></div><input id="w-feas" aria-label="可完成性" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="30"></div><div class="weight-row"><div class="weight-top"><span>研究深度 · Research depth</span><output id="w-depth-out">20</output></div><input id="w-depth" aria-label="研究深度" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="20"></div><div class="weight-row"><div class="weight-top"><span>作品集价值 · Portfolio</span><output id="w-career-out">15</output></div><input id="w-career" aria-label="作品集价值" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="15"></div><button class="btn ghost small" onclick="resetWeights()" style="margin-top:10px">↺ 回到默认权重 / Reset</button><div class="score-legend">评分方式：每项先做 1–5 分的规划判断，再乘以权重换算成 100 分。风险与训练资源仍建议通过前期 smoke test 亲自验证。<span class="en">Each criterion is rated 1–5 and weighted into a /100 score. Risk and compute estimates are preliminary.</span></div></aside><div class="surface rank-table-wrap"><table class="rank-table"><thead><tr><th>RANK</th><th>研究方向 / Project</th><th>课程 / Course</th><th>可行 / Feasibility</th><th>深度 / Depth</th><th>风险 / Risk</th><th style="min-width:142px">TOTAL / 100</th></tr></thead><tbody id="ranking-body"></tbody></table></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="topics"><div class="container"><div class="section-header"><div><div class="eyebrow">FIVE RESEARCH BLUEPRINTS</div><h2>每一个选题，<br>都值得认真想想。</h2></div><p>点开任意卡片，都可以看到更完整的研究蓝图：问题、假设、数据集、技术变化、对照实验、评价指标，以及遇到风险时可以怎样温和收缩范围。<span class="en">Open any card to explore a fuller research blueprint, including the question, hypothesis, dataset, controlled experiments, metrics, and a graceful fallback plan.</span></p></div><div class="topic-grid" id="topic-grid"></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="roadmap"><div class="container"><div class="section-header"><div><div class="eyebrow">EXECUTION ROADMAP</div><h2>让节奏留一点余裕，<br>把重要的事慢慢做好。</h2></div><p>下面是一份可调整的建议节奏图，方便你们把自己的推进计划和课程节点放在一起看。蓝色代表组员 A，紫色代表组员 B，绿色代表双方共同推进。<span class="en">This adjustable roadmap is a planning companion, designed to sit alongside the course schedule. Blue = Member A, violet = Member B, and green = shared work.</span></p></div><div class="course-milestones surface"><div class="milestone-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">COURSE MILESTONES</div><h3>课程关键节点</h3><p>下面这些日期来自你提供的课程日历截图。它们可以和团队自己的节奏图放在一起看，帮助大家既不慌张，也不遗漏关键提交。<span class="en">These dates come from your course calendar screenshot and can be viewed alongside the team roadmap to keep the pace calm and clear.</span></p></div><div class="pill gray">Canvas / syllabus still takes priority</div></div><div class="milestone-grid" id="course-milestones"></div></div><div class="surface gantt-shell"><div class="gantt-controls"><div><label>项目开始日期 / Start date <input type="date" id="gantt-start" value="2026-10-30"></label></div><div><label>显示负责人 / Owner <select id="owner-filter"><option value="all">全部 / All</option><option value="a">Member A</option><option value="b">Member B</option><option value="both">Joint / 双方</option></select></label></div></div><div style="overflow:auto"><div class="gantt-grid"><div class="gantt-head" id="gantt-head"></div><div id="gantt-body"></div></div></div><div class="legend-line"><span><i class="legend-dot"></i>Member A · 数据/评估</span><span><i class="legend-dot b"></i>Member B · 模型/训练</span><span><i class="legend-dot both"></i>Joint · 双方合作</span><span>▬ 先把 Baseline 站稳，再慢慢叠加改动 · Baseline first</span></div><div class="warning-strip" style="margin-top:23px">节奏建议：如果到第 2 周末 Baseline 还没有稳定复现，不妨温和地收缩题目范围，先把项目做稳。正式日期仍请以 Canvas 的 Project Deliverables 为准。<span class="en">If the baseline is not reproducible by the end of Week 2, narrow scope and activate the fallback. Update dates from Canvas.</span></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="requirements"><div class="container"><div class="section-header"><div><div class="eyebrow">OFFICIAL REQUIREMENTS · PDF PP. 1–7</div><h2>把课程要求，<br>安静地一项项对齐。</h2></div><p>这里整理的是你上传的 7 页指南中最关键的六项技术要求，以及老师明确不希望看到的低深度项目形式。<span class="en">Below is a calm summary of the six technical pillars in your uploaded guideline, along with the low-depth project patterns the course discourages.</span></p></div><div class="requirements-grid" id="requirements-grid"></div><div class="eyebrow" style="margin:30px 0 12px">WHAT DOES NOT QUALIFY · PDF PP. 2–3</div><div class="bad-grid"><div class="bad"><b>✕ 教程式复现</b><span>Tutorial-only implementation<br>仅照搬已有教程代码</span></div><div class="bad"><b>✕ 简单跑榜</b><span>Benchmark-only comparison<br>只比较多个模型准确率</span></div><div class="bad"><b>✕ 纯文献综述</b><span>Literature survey only<br>没有实质技术贡献</span></div><div class="bad"><b>✕ 只调用预训练模型</b><span>Inference-only application<br>缺少修改与分析</span></div></div><div class="footer-banner"><div><h3>把诚信与复现，也放进项目的气质里。</h3><p>代码需由团队完成，外部代码必须注明来源与修改。AI 可用于概念学习或调试，但不能提交自己无法解释的生成成果。<br>Team-owned work, proper attribution and explainable implementation are mandatory. AI assistance for concepts/debugging is allowed by the guideline.</p></div><a href="#kickoff" class="btn">去看看会议清单 ↗</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="kickoff"><div class="container"><div class="section-header"><div><div class="eyebrow">TEAM KICKOFF TOOLKIT</div><h2>第一次 Zoom，<br>可以一起聊清什么？</h2></div><p>如果希望第一次线上会议既轻松又有收获，可以参考下面这套 Kickoff 节奏：把问题、计划、分工和接下来 48 小时的下一步慢慢聊清楚。<span class="en">If you want your first Zoom to feel both relaxed and productive, this kickoff flow helps the team leave with clarity, ownership, and a gentle next step.</span></p></div><div class="meeting-layout"><div class="surface meeting-card"><h3>会议议程 · 70 minutes</h3><div class="en">Suggested meeting agenda</div><div id="agenda"></div></div><div class="surface meeting-card"><h3>共识清单 · Decision log</h3><div class="en">As ideas settle, you can tick each item here. Checkmarks are saved in this browser.</div><div class="progress-track"><div class="progress-fill" id="check-progress"></div></div><div style="font-size:11px;color:#8b8b90;margin-bottom:12px" id="check-count">0 / 10 decisions confirmed</div><div id="kickoff-checks"></div><button class="btn ghost small" style="margin-top:19px" onclick="copyMinutes()">复制会议纪要模板 / Copy notes ↗</button></div></div></div></section>
